{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And Moses returned the words of the people to YHWH</b> — that he returned before Him to the mountain with the people's answer. And behold, all is revealed before Him, yet He did not ask him, \"What did this people answer you?\" — as in the verse, \"And YHWH heard the sound of your words when you spoke to me\" (Deuteronomy 5:24). And when he came before Him, HaShem, blessed be He, said: <b>Behold, I come to you in the thickness of the cloud, so that the people may hear when I speak with you, and also in you they will believe forever</b>. Then Moses said before Him: Master of the Universe, Your children are believers and they accept upon themselves all that You will speak. And similarly, \"they returned to them with a report and showed them the fruit of the land\" (Numbers 13:26) — they returned to them along with the things they saw, for afterward it says, \"and they told him and said\". And there is no need for the words of Rabbi Abraham (Ibn Ezra) on this."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:10:45.702289161Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}